  "description": "A lossless hologram for .NET. CycleHologram stores a multiset on a finite field in a fixed 2k+1 eight-byte elements and returns every symbol and count exactly up to capacity k, refusing past it. Holograms add and subtract exactly, so two replicas find precisely what differs by exchanging one hologram sized to the difference. Beneath it, the phasor Vector Symbolic Architecture (VSA) codec: bind, unbind, bundle and correlate over unit-complex faces, with a fixed frozen-identity codec for models and a width-configurable SIMD codec for storage and similarity search. The shared substrate under Evaluated Applications' holographic database and phasor model library.",
